course: dictionary
lesson: 7291
title: Meet the pipistrelle
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pipistrelle is a kind of bat. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it: «A tiny pipistrelle, lighter than a coin, can eat around 3,000 small insects in one night.» Tiny and lighter than a coin tell you it is very small, and eating insects tells you what it does.
explain: Pipistrelles find food in the dark using echolocation. The bat sends out squeaks and listens for the echoes that bounce back from insects, so it can find them even on a dark night.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «A tiny bat, lighter than a coin, can eat around 3,000 small insects in one night.» It still makes sense, so you have understood the word.
fact: A pipistrelle is a very small bat, and the commonest bat in Britain and much of Europe.
fact: «The common pipistrelle weighs about 5 grams, less than a pound coin.»
fact: A pipistrelle may eat thousands of tiny insects, such as midges and mosquitoes, in one night.
fact: Pipistrelles can squeeze through a gap about 1 centimetre wide.
fact: In the UK, bats are protected by law, so you must not disturb their roosts.
exercise: What is a pipistrelle? | A large bird that hunts fish | *A very small bat | A type of moth that glows | A tree that grows near rivers
exercise: Pipistrelles find insects in the dark by echolocation. What does echolocation mean? | Flying only when the wind is strong | Hiding under streetlights | Seeing with very bright eyes | *Sending out squeaks and listening for the echoes
exercise: «The common pipistrelle weighs about 5 grams, less than a pound coin.» How much does it weigh? | About 500 grams | *About 5 grams | About 50 grams | About 5 kilograms
test: What do pipistrelles eat? | Mice from the barn | Seeds and berries | *Tiny insects such as midges and mosquitoes | Fish from the river
test: Bats are protected by law in the UK. What must you do with a bat's roost? | Move it to a warmer place | Take the bats home as pets | *Leave it alone and do not disturb it | Shine a torch inside to look
exam: In «The common pipistrelle is Britain's commonest bat», what does commonest mean? | Rarest, found in only a few places | Biggest of all bats | Fastest flying bat | *Most common, found in the most places
